# Checkpoints and model weights
checkpoints/
runs/
*.ckpt
*.pt
*.pth
*.safetensors
*.bin

# Datasets and TFDS builds
data/
datasets/
tensorflow_datasets/
tfds/
*.tfrecord
*.tfrecord-*
*.parquet

# Videos and rendered output. Rollout videos are regenerable from a run and are large,
# so they stay out -- but the two GIFs the README displays are release artefacts and must
# be committed, or the README renders a blank box. `git add -A` skips ignored files
# silently, which is exactly how they were missed the first time.
videos/
*.mp4
*.avi
*.gif
*.webm
!docs/media/*.gif

# Profiles and traces
traces/
*.nsys-rep
*.sqlite
*.qdrep
*.ncu-rep
*.json.gz
*.pt.trace.json

# Logs
logs/
*.log

# Arrays. gitignore has no size predicate, so .npz/.npy are excluded by
# default; add a small one deliberately with `git add -f <path>`.
*.npz
*.npy
# Exception: the fitted probe (88 KB) is what RuntimeMonitor loads by default and what
# EVAL.md documents as the shipped operating point. Without it in the tree a clone cannot
# run MONITOR=log or MONITOR=stop at all. tests/test_release_artefacts.py enforces this.
!bench/out/m7b_probe.npz

# Conda / virtual envs
envs/
# Exception: envs/ at the REPO ROOT is the environment specs, not an installed env --
# conda env export + pip freeze + BUILD.md, which is the only record of how to rebuild
# planner, libero-vla and learn-gpu. `git add -A` skips ignored files silently, which is
# how the README GIFs were missed the first time; these must not go the same way.
!envs/
!envs/*.yml
!envs/*.requirements.txt
!envs/BUILD.md
env/
venv/
.venv/
conda-env/
miniconda3/
anaconda3/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.so
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Experiment tracking
wandb/

# Audit artefacts: raw profiles, traces and timing arrays stay on disk (plan section 9).
# The summarised JSON they produce is committed; these are the multi-hundred-MB originals.
*.prof
*.sqlite
*.nsys-rep
*_trace.json
audit/t1_out/
audit/t2_out/
audit/t3_out/
audit/DONE
audit/FAILED
audit/SUMMARY.txt
audit/M0_AUDIT_*
audit/M2_*
audit/logs/

# Benchmark measurement records (small JSON) ARE committed -- they are the provenance for
# every number in DESIGN.md, and tests/test_gjk_real_states.py gates one of them. Only the
# bulky per-call arrays are excluded, by the *.npz rule above. The compiled extension is
# already excluded by the *.so rule in the Python section.
bench/runs/
bench/triton_libs/
.ruff_cache/

# Milestone 7a planner: the vendored cuRobo checkout (189 MB, a git clone of NVlabs/curobo at
# tag v0.7.6) is a third-party dependency, not our code -- FEASIBILITY.md records the tag and
# the build flags so it can be re-cloned. Saved joint paths and plan arrays are artefacts.
fastvla/planner/third_party/
fastvla/planner/out/
